{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact integration head 9be94e8c697d44404ad1a85e0d8e91eb1f5e9e5f (one commit atop the merged setup gap closure b2969cc; not on main), for one test-coverage condition of the operator umbrella #2272; everything else is verified. VERIFIED AGAINST #2272: the rendered upgrade.sh release asset (pinned like install.sh, in both checksum manifests, checked by the PR dry-run) downloads checksums.txt, its Cosign signature and bundle, and install.sh from the pinned release, verifies the installer checksum before executing it (and the keyless identity for the exact tag when cosign is present), then stages the verified release through install.sh --bundles none --no-service into the versioned user-owned directory; it records the known-good prior target at lib/tailapp/tailapp.previous, atomically switches the stable link, restarts launchd (kickstart) or systemd --user (daemon-reload + restart), waits for control-plane health, and on failure restores the prior link and restarts again; --rollback selects the recorded prior binary explicitly. It distinguishes a healthy control plane from ingestion_ready and reports machine-readably: one JSON line with control_plane, ingestion_ready, action upgraded or upgrade_pending, and next (apps status plus the exact Upgrading guide) - a runtime-profile hold is reported as an expected app-upgrade requirement, never as a failed binary upgrade, and nothing auto-reactivates. By default it installs no bundles, rewrites no source, activates nothing, resets nothing, and changes no telemetry configuration (a second resident on a served home is refused by the engine.lock flock, so the installer temporary-resident path is inert during an upgrade). Docs: resident-upgrade.md now leads with the release upgrader and its JSON semantics, keeping the checkout script as a separate non-consumer path; releases.md and README updated. Clean worktree: go build/vet OK, go test 15 packages ok (scripts 20.5 s), go test -race 15